# Deploying Streamlit on Hostinger (hPanel)

There are two main types of hosting on Hostinger: **Shared/Cloud Web Hosting** and **VPS Hosting**. Streamlit works very differently on each.

## ⚠️ Important: Shared vs. VPS Hosting
**Streamlit apps create a continuous running server**, unlike standard PHP/WordPress sites that only run when a user visits a page.
- **Shared / Cloud Web Hosting**: usually **DOES NOT support Streamlit** natively. You generally cannot open custom ports (like 8501) and long-running background processes are often killed by the server.
- **VPS Hosting**: This is **required** to run Streamlit on Hostinger. You get full control to install Python, open ports, and keep the app running.

---

## Scenario A: I have a VPS Plan (Recommended)
If you have a VPS plan, follow these steps to deploy your app:

1. **SSH into your VPS**:
   Use the Terminal in hPanel or your local terminal:
   ```bash
   ssh root@your-server-ip
   ```

2. **Update and Install Docker**:
   ```bash
   apt-get update
   apt-get install docker.io -y
   ```

3. **Upload your files**:
   You can use SFTP (FileZilla) or `scp` to copy [app.py](file:///Users/shreekant/.gemini/antigravity/brain/660b5934-1c3a-417f-85f2-433e7a14ae5a/app.py), [requirements.txt](file:///Users/shreekant/.gemini/antigravity/brain/660b5934-1c3a-417f-85f2-433e7a14ae5a/requirements.txt), [Dockerfile](file:///Users/shreekant/.gemini/antigravity/brain/660b5934-1c3a-417f-85f2-433e7a14ae5a/Dockerfile), and [column_mapping.md](file:///Users/shreekant/.gemini/antigravity/brain/660b5934-1c3a-417f-85f2-433e7a14ae5a/column_mapping.md) to a folder like `/root/dashboard`.

4. **Build and Run**:
   Navigate to the folder and run:
   ```bash
   cd /root/dashboard
   docker build -t dropship-dashboard .
   docker run -d -p 80:8501 --restart always dropship-dashboard
   ```
   *Note: We mapped port 80 to 8501 so you can access it directly via your IP/Domain without `:8501`.*

---

## Scenario B: I have Shared/Cloud Hosting (Standard)
If you are on a standard plan, you cannot easily run Streamlit directly. The "Python App" feature in hPanel is designed for WSGI apps (Flask/Django), not Streamlit.

### Best Alternative: Streamlit Community Cloud (Free)
Since you cannot run the server process on Shared hosting, the best way is to host the app for free on Streamlit Cloud and link it to your domain.

1. **Upload your code to GitHub**.
2. Go to [share.streamlit.io](https://share.streamlit.io) and sign in.
3. Click **"New App"** and select your GitHub repository.
4. Once deployed, you will get a URL (e.g., `https://your-app.streamlit.app`).
5. **Embed in your Hostinger Website**:
   If you have a main website on Hostinger, you can embed the dashboard using an iframe:
   ```html
   <iframe src="https://your-app.streamlit.app" width="100%" height="800px"></iframe>
   ```
